{\*\generator Msftedit 5.41.15.1515;}\viewkind4\uc1\pard\f0\fs20 Here's some quick notes about the characters, for you to use when you get to code them. It should be enough for three custom characters: if the campaign ever features more, I will note of them separately.\par
\par
I don't expect you to cram all this information into game: plenty of it will remain as background information, that most players will never find out unless they ask us directly about it.\par
\par
---\par
Cheska Kuhral:\par
- Overview: Young, smart, tough female commander. Wears heavy armor and carries heavy weaponry, very much against the norm of female warriors.\par
* Skills and traits:\par
** Leadership: She is the main character, after all, and specifically trained for this duty.\par
** Strong: To use all that heavy equipment of hers, Cheska would have to be in much better fit than your average trooper, female or not.\par
** Intelligent: Already in her training, she was noted as being especially smart, cunning, skilled tactician, and fast learner.\par
* Resistances: Exactly the same as heavy infantryman.\par
\par
- Level 1: Noblewoman\par
* Description: Nobles in Wesnoth are often trained in art of war and commanding their own armies, then knighted and sent to the battlefield to lead the peasants and commoners into battle. These young bluebloods often lack of actual battle experience: the pride and arrogance they often feel towards the "lesser people" they're commanding, and insisting on being in charge even when their more experienced subordinates could handle the job better, often results in quite impressive military disasters. Cheska Kuhral has managed to evade most of these traps, however, growing up into much more pleasant and humble than many of her peers.\par
* HP: 30\par
* Movement: 5\par
* XP: 35\par
* Weapons:\par
** Zweih\'e4nder: Cheska's most prominent weapon was inherited from her father. It is a gigantic sword, six feet tall, that has been told to be able to decapitate several men in a single blow. 10 - 2 (blade, melee)\par
** Crossbow: Although not as skilled in using this weapon than her sword, Cheska can defend herself in a ranged combat. 10 - 1 (pierce, ranged)\par
\par
- Level 2: Amazon\par
* Description: Perhaps not technically a member of the legendary all-female warband from the far past, Cheska does fit the general description very well, and could probably have stood along its members in a battle, had she been born several thousand years ago in entirely another human empire. But she did not, so this is the nearest she will get in that regard.\par
* HP: 37\par
* Movement: 5\par
* XP: 82\par
* Weapons:\par
** Zweih\'e4nder: 14 - 2 (blade, melee)\par
** Crossbow: 14 - 1 (pierce, ranged)\par
\par
- Level 3: Warmistress\par
* Description: Her force now consisting of several different armies and factions, Cheska has been given this honorary title by her troops, representing the supreme commander of all armies and units in a war, effectively the entire battleforce of a large interracial alliance. She does not officially hold the title, of course - no one has been given this honor for several centuries, not since the last Warmaster, a man named Horus, threatened to incite men and elves in a rebellion against Wesnoth and the surrounding countries, that would have torn the nations apart had he not been assassinated in the early days of the revolt.\par
* HP: 47\par
* Movement: 6\par
* XP: 200\par
* Weapons:\par
** Zweih\'e4nder: 20 - 2 (blade, melee)\par
** Morningstar: Cheska is expanding her weaponry in an effort to become more capable against different kinds of foes, especially undead. This weapon is faster than her primary weapon, but not quite as devastating. 14 - 3 (impact, melee)\par
** Crossbow: 20 - 1 (pierce, ranged)\par
\par
- Level 4: Lady'O'War\par
* Description: Perhaps it is peaceful in most of Wesnoth, allowing many battle commanders and generals to grow idle, but Cheska Kuhral has seen a great deal of warfare in that same time. Still young, idealistic, and somewhat naive, she regardless holds enough skill and authority - combined with cunning, intelligence, and empathy towards her troops - to be counted equal among those other men, those who have not seen serious battle since the Turmoil of Asheviere.\par
* HP: 60\par
* Movement: 6\par
* XP: 150\par
* Weapons:\par
** Zweih\'e4nder: The mastery of her weapon has made Cheska capable of using it even faster. 20 - 3 (blade, melee)\par
** Morningstar: 20 - 3 (impact, melee)\par
** Crossbow: Although she is still utilizing her mighty sword as her primary weapon, by this point Cheska has become very skilled and very accurate with her crossbow as well. 30 - 1 (pierce, ranger, marksman)\par
\par
---\par
Silan Abner:\par
- Overview: A wanderer of indeterminate age, using the dark arts of necromancy in his one-man war against the enemies of Wesnoth. His past and motives still remain largely unclear.\par
* Skills and traits:\par
** Fearless: Although he has delved into forsaken magic, Silan never entirely abandoned sun, and can stand in daylight without flinching when other necromancers and undead would cover themselves, screaming.\par
** Loyal: Cheska may be quite wary of him at first, because of necromancy and the like, but Silan himself put his full trust to the woman from the very beginning.\par
* Resistances: Being based on necromancers, he has the same resistances they have.\par
\par
- Level 1: Loner\par
* Description: In general sense, humans seek each other's company, and most often live and work in groups. It is a remnant of the ancient days, perhaps, when teamwork was the only thing that allowed mankind to survive. Regardless, there are some individuals who would much rather remain alone and fend for themselves - or perhaps the society itself cast them away, for one reason or another.\par
* HP: 30\par
* Movement: 5\par
* XP: 45\par
* Weapons:\par
** Staff: Nothing but a long piece of wood, Silan usually employs it as a tool to help him walk the treacherous mountain paths - but it does still hurt when he bashes it to someone's head hard enough. 4 - 3 (impact, melee)\par
** Chill Wave: 12 - 2 (cold, ranged, magical)\par
** Shadow Wave: 8 - 2 (arcane, ranged, magical)\par
\par
- Level 2: Hermit\par
* Description: Living in their caves, far from the reach of man and civilization, searching for personal peace and enlightenment, hermits can live years or even decades without a single human contact. This does not hold true for Silan Abner, of course, but the other general attributes still stand.\par
* HP: 52\par
* Movement: 6\par
* XP: 85\par
* Weapons:\par
** Staff: 5 - 3 (impact, melee)\par
** Chill Wave: 15 - 2 (cold, ranged, magical)\par
** Shadow Wave: 11 - 2 (arcane, ranged, magical)\par
\par
- Level 3: Solitaire\par
* Description: No one knows what secrets universe can reveal to a man when he shuns other human contact and escaped them to the wilderness, but it is clear that the decades Silan has spent by himself, have taught him much. The occasional bits of insight he chooses to sometimes reveal to his companions are but the tip of the iceberg of all the knowledge he has gathered within his brain.\par
* HP: 74\par
* Movement: 6\par
* XP: 140\par
* Weapons:\par
** Staff: 7 - 3 (impact, melee)\par
** Chill Wave: 20 - 2 (cold, ranged, magical)\par
** Shadow Wave: 15 - 2 (arcane, ranged, magical)\par
\par
---\par
Xel:\par
- Overview: A saurian runaway from far east, bearing scars and shackled as a reminder of whatever abuse he used to face in his homeland. A capable, opportunistic, but slightly cowardly warrior.\par
* Skills and traits:\par
** Ambush: Xel is a native to the swamplands, and can hide himself expertly in there, remaining out of sight of absolutely everybody unless they stand right next to him.\par
** Backstab: Pragmatist in nature, even to greater extent than your average saurian, Xel will take every opportunity for a surprise attack. Turn your back to a conniving lizard and you deserve what you get.\par
** Quick: Even with the shackles weighing him down, Xel can outrun most other saurians. Without his speed could perhaps rival a horse, but with far more dexterity and maneuverability.\par
** Loyal: Xel recognizes a superior commander when he sees one, and realizes that under Cheska's command, he has far higher chance to survive and prosper. He has become fast friends with her since, and has grown unusually attached to her.\par
** Encumbered: Unfortunately, with his shackles hindering him, Xel has difficulties in balancing himself for ranged combat. As such, when attacking or defending himself from afar, the accuracy of his attacks can never exceed 60%.\par
* Resistances: Same as saurian skirmisher and its upgrades.\par
\par
- Level 1: Runaway\par
* Description: This saurian has a past of captivity. Whether imprisoned for crime or slavery, he has since broken free, and has absolutely no intentions of getting captured again. Adding the natural size and agility to his general dislike in being held in one place against his will, has made him extremely unrestrained and unpredictable.\par
* HP: 24\par
* Movement: 6\par
* XP: 30\par
* Weapons:\par
** Spear: 5 - 4 (pierce, melee)\par
** Chain: This is the piece of iron chain that used to hold Xel's arms together. It has been enchanted with powerful magics, to keep the captive from breaking out of it - which Xel nonetheless managed to do. The magic is still there, resulting in quite a fast and powerful weapon. 2 - 5 (impact, melee, magical)\par
** Spear: 4 - 2 (pierce, ranged)\par
\par
- Level 2: Escapee\par
* Description: Many runaways are eventually captured and brought back to justice (or their owners): those that manage to elude this grim fate evidently become highly skilled at it. Experienced at avoiding authorities, he can slip past any gap in your defenses, as small and unnoticeable as ever, and slip back into the night, never to be found again.\par
* HP: 32\par
* Movement: 7\par
* XP: 51\par
* Weapons:\par
** Spear: 7 - 4 (pierce, melee)\par
** Flail: The addition of a spiked ball to the end of the chain might have made this weapon slightly slower, but the resulting increase in effect more than makes up for it. 9 - 3 (impact, melee, magical)\par
** Spear: 5 - 2 (pierce, ranged)\par
\par
- Level 3: Unfettered\par
* Description: The very epitome of freedom and independence, this is a saurian that can go practically everywhere he wants, do anything he wants, and get away with it. He has truly freed himself from all boundaries of reality that hold most others captive: money or status do not interest him, laws or judges can not stop him, traps and cages will not even slow him down.\par
* HP: 43\par
* Movement: 7\par
* XP: 150\par
* Weapons:\par
** Spear: 10 - 4 (pierce, melee)\par
** Flail: 12 - 3 (impact, melee, magical)\par
** Spear: 7 - 2 (pierce, ranged)\par
}
